      "title": "Australia news live: Westpac accuses KPMG of ‘drip feeding’ information on alleged leaks; Qantas refunds passengers stranded in Johannesburg for two nights",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/14/australia-news-live-kpmg-inquiry-icac-alan-jones-trial-gst-treasurer-jim-chalmers-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-labor-liberals-one-nation-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Follow today’s news live</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p><strong>Albanese says gambling inducements are ‘over the top’</strong></p><p>Albanese said gambling inducements are “over the top and need to be wound back”.</p><p>Look, we’re working constructively across the parliament to put in place these reforms. They are important.</p><p>The problem is addiction and when someone has an addiction, if there are inducements that are encouraging that addiction, that’s a bad thing. There’s nothing wrong with people having a punt on a Saturday … the problem is if it’s an addiction.</p><p>We agreed it was a project that is and will continue to deliver benefits for the United States, for Australia, and for the United Kingdom.</p><p>I always put forward Australia’s national interest during these discussions.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/14/australia-news-live-kpmg-inquiry-icac-alan-jones-trial-gst-treasurer-jim-chalmers-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-labor-liberals-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-14T00:49:06"
    },
    {
      "title": "One Nation staffer accused of posing as leftwing content creator in ‘undercover’ videos",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/14/one-nation-staffer-accused-of-posing-as-leftwing-content-creator-in-undercover-videos-ntwnfb",
      "description": "<p>Exclusive: The videos, filmed at anti-One Nation rallies, were posted to party’s social pages and appear to be endorsed by Pauline Hanson</p><ul><li><p><a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/live/2026/aug/14/australia-news-live-kpmg-inquiry-icac-alan-jones-trial-gst-treasurer-jim-chalmers-anthony-albanese-angus-taylor-pauline-hanson-labor-liberals-one-nation-ntwnfb\">Follow our Australia news live blog for latest updates</a></p></li><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>The owners of a progressive social media page have accused One Nation of impersonating them at anti-Pauline Hanson rallies while shooting a series of “undercover” videos.</p><p>Hanson’s party has recently published a string of videos with a young male host attending leftwing protests. In the clips – published on pages owned by One Nation and Hanson on Instagram, TikTok and X – a party staffer seeks to embarrass protesters in filmed interviews.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/2026/aug/14/one-nation-staffer-accused-of-posing-as-leftwing-content-creator-in-undercover-videos-ntwnfb\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-13T15:00:04"
    },
    {
      "title": "Is Australia’s buy now, pay later boom at an end?",
      "link": "https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/aug/14/is-australias-buy-now-pay-later-boom-at-an-end",
      "description": "<p>Several firms promised to disrupt the consumer credit market by offering consumers their purchases instantly and the bill later. Did it work?</p><ul><li><p>Get our <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/email-newsletters?CMP=cvau_sfl\">breaking news email</a>, <a href=\"https://app.adjust.com/w4u7jx3\">free app</a> or <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/australia-news/series/full-story?CMP=cvau_sfl\">daily news podcast</a></p></li></ul><p>Afterpay has never turned a profit in Australia. Last month, it spent millions to take over a Sydney Olympic Park arena.</p><p>The company says Afterpay Arena will be the first venue where Australians can “buy now, pay later” for their event tickets, merchandise, dinner and even alcohol.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/business/2026/aug/14/is-australias-buy-now-pay-later-boom-at-an-end\">Continue reading...</a>",
      "source_name": "The Guardian World",
      "published": "2026-08-13T15:00:03"
    }
